"Temporary per-transaction state belongs in SpacetimeDB EVENT tables (native, transient per transaction, indexable on entity id), never as temporary fields on real components. Read the table back within the transaction so repeated application is idempotent (new application = target minus already-applied); no reset system is needed because event rows do not persist past the transaction. First model: HP share — hp_share_system copies each partner's per-tick HP deltas (accumulated_damage/healing) onto the entity's own deltas via an entity-id-indexed event table, in a compute pass then an update pass, NEVER modifying hp directly so deltas stay truthful for other systems. To be generalized into a reusable 'transient component' mechanism."